loadguardreads_x86_64 -- the GH-1034 LOAD guard fixture for option `loadguardreads`
(tests/stages/kuna-loadguardreads.xml).

What it is
  A 24,224-byte x86-64 ELF built from loadguardreads_x86_64.c, which is
  generated straight-line C. `gather` hands the address of its 64-word table
  `t` and of each of 64 stack structs to `reg`, so every stack slot is
  address-tied, then reads `t` at 256 data-dependent indexes: 256 indexed stack
  LOADs that heritage guards against every address-tied stack range.

Why it is vendored
  The op counts the stage test pins depend on the exact code layout, so the
  binary is checked in rather than built at test time (CI's gcc 15 would lay the
  function out differently).

Where it came from
  gcc 11.4.0 (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.3), GNU ld 2.38, x86-64 Linux:

      gcc -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie -fno-inline -fstack-reuse=none -o loadguardreads_x86_64 loadguardreads_x86_64.c

  sha256 2e158e856298d176b68e5661ba0bb37de8e23da930354e776b045dca9600382b.
  Run with no arguments it prints 100734.
